    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59653" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρᾰπᾰτᾰλός </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραπαταλλός</span></b>  Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.158
		</span></i>), ὁ, a worthless kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fish</i>, hence 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωρός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κραπαταλοί</span>, title of play
			by Pherecrates, in which he says that the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραπαταλός</span> is used for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δραχμή</span> in Hades, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				9.83
			</span></i>.</div>
